GridSimEnv data: terms and sources

This file covers the task packs under data/ (ercot-dam-v1-train, ercot-dam-v1-eval, ercot-dam-v1-eval-iid,
ercot-dam-v1-rtcb, showcase and fixtures: tasks.jsonl.gz and manifest.json), data/stats.md and data/ridge-v1.json, and
everything derived from them: the prompts, situations, references, schedules, Episode JSON and transcripts this
repository writes, and the Hugging Face dataset earakely-scale/GridSimEnv-AgentEnv. The code is Apache-2.0 (LICENSE);
NOTICE lists every source.

1. ERCOT prices: ERCOT's terms, not relicensed

Every price in the packs, and every number derived from them, comes from public data of the Electric Reliability
Council of Texas, Inc. (ERCOT): report NP4-180-ER, "Historical DAM Load Zone and Hub Prices" (report type 13060),
https://www.ercot.com/mp/data-products/data-product-details?id=NP4-180-ER, the yearly files DAMLZHBSPP_2014.zip to
DAMLZHBSPP_2026.zip, whose SHA-256 each pack's manifest.json records.

The ERCOT data is used, reproduced and redistributed under ERCOT's Website User Agreement, section 5 below, as a
compilation and analysis of raw data provided in public portions of ercot.com. It is not relicensed: neither this file
nor the Apache-2.0 licence of the code nor any Creative Commons licence applies to it, and anyone who uses it is bound
by ERCOT's terms. ERCOT does not guarantee the accuracy of this compilation. Source: ERCOT. GridSimEnv is not
affiliated with or endorsed by ERCOT. The ERCOT logo, "ERCOT" and "The Texas Connection" are trademarks of ERCOT
(section 9); this repository uses none of them beyond naming the source.

